perfcached is licensed in two parts, on purpose.

THE DAEMON - everything that links src/core/ (the server, its cluster
plane, the CLI, the tests and benches) - is licensed under the GNU
General Public License, version 2 or (at your option) any later
version.  The full text is in COPYING.  src/core/ is shared with the
OpenSIPS cachedb_perf module and carries its own GPL-2.0-or-later
headers; the same terms cover the rest of the daemon.

THE CLIENT LIBRARY - libperfd - is licensed under the MIT License (see
lib/LICENSE), so it can be embedded in software under any license,
proprietary included.  The MIT-licensed set is exactly:

    lib/perfd.c  lib/perfd.h
    src/json.c   src/json.h
    src/pc_noise.c  src/pc_noise.h
    src/pc_slot.h   src/pc_mix.h

These files include nothing from src/core/ (verified, and kept that
way: tools/sync-libperfd.sh exports precisely this set to consumers).

Every file carries an SPDX-License-Identifier stating which side it is
on; files without one are daemon-side, GPL-2.0-or-later.

